   "draft": {
    "headline": "Jake White starts on the ground where Fiji lost the final",
    "beats": [
     "Fiji appointed Jake White in October from 31 applicants, replacing interim coach Senirusi Seruvakula. His first Test is against the Japan side that beat them 20–15 in the Pacific Nations Cup final on 19 September, at this same ground in Tokyo.",
     "Fiji's only win this year came against Canada, and England put 73 on them in July. Japan have won three straight, scoring 63 against the USA and 57 against Canada before the final.",
     "White, 62, has a pragmatic reputation, but Fiji's rugby boss says the flair stays. The Blue Bulls president put it more bluntly: \"I think Fiji needs its South African discipline.\"",
     "Win, and Fiji go back above Japan. Lose, and they drop below Wales, which is where Japan go next."
    ],
